    fix(DF-0926-06): validate key format before rememberTool, return 400 not 500
    
    POST /api/memories with a key missing the leading slash (e.g.
    "examples/http/test") was falling through to rememberTool which threw
    a 500. Add an explicit validation check that throws ValidationError
    (mapped to 400) before the rememberTool call.
    
    Add integration test http-key-validation.int.test.ts asserting 400
    for missing-slash keys and 201 for valid keys.
    
    ch:trace row=DF-0926-06 evidence=tests/http-key-validation.int.test.ts witness=live:integration-test-2/2-green commit=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
---
 src/http/routes/memories.ts           |  7 ++++++
 tests/http-key-validation.int.test.ts | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 54 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/http/routes/memories.ts b/src/http/routes/memories.ts
index b6162f7..40fa508 100644
--- a/src/http/routes/memories.ts
+++ b/src/http/routes/memories.ts
@@ -689,6 +689,13 @@ router.post(
       );
     }
 
+    // DF-0926-06: validate key format before it reaches rememberTool
+    if (!body.key.startsWith("/")) {
+      throw new ValidationError(
+        `Invalid key '${body.key}': key must be a filesystem-style path starting with / (e.g., /projects/mcp)`,
+      );
+    }
+
     // Call rememberTool to create memory
     // DB-GAP-031: an authenticated principal stamps the record — a
     // client-supplied ?author= or body author is never honored on writes.
